    {
      "id": "claim_c3dfd045a39045ca80cf8b4359981f41",
      "statement": "After auth the relay branches on role: extension sockets handle browser_presence_announce, extension_keepalive, and routed responses, while mcp sockets handle list_browsers (answered from memory) and forward all other payloads (including list_tabs) to a selected browser.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/websocket/src/server.ts#L186-L209",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:793bea5ca1b245043b7dc141b2c592e9cb25a1140c2d67dbce69930efd097b68:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/websocket/src/server.ts#L211-L275",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5fc858858147b67b737f71a83bf21b64966d16cedbb34a58da23c7012624c11d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/websocket/src/server.ts#L342-L391",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5771850a4a71efd6d3b965c1acf917e74d73d94d2926684358aa166355304cfe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_74b77c1c81f5420f9bc3ef4a8d2238ad",
      "statement": "MCP request targeting is explicit and per-call via message.target.browserInstanceId: an explicit id that misses returns browser_unavailable; no target with zero online browsers returns browser_unavailable; no target with multiple browsers returns ambiguous_browser_target with the candidate list; otherwise the unique/explicit browser is selected. tabId is passed through verbatim and not interpreted, and no selected-browser session state persists between requests.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/protocol.ts#L4-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b81719843781cc7a2d1c94892d3f561dcd84f12e813b852b5eaa17ef6f2d78cd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/websocket/src/server.test.ts#L213-L305",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7bb9663b817e8db4159a173d0993c529b6f7ef98688b263074e0d65cfc54d7b9:"
        },
        {
